# Design System Tokens

All color and typography values in CSS, SCSS, and Tailwind must use design-system tokens defined in `src/styles/tokens.css` and `src/styles/globals.css`. Never hard-code values when a token exists.

## Color: use `--ds-*` tokens, not mapped aliases

`globals.css` defines shorthand aliases (`--foreground`, `--background`, `--card`, etc.) that map to `--ds-*` tokens. **Do not use the aliases in component styles.** Use the `--ds-*` tokens directly so the intent is explicit and grep-able.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — mapped alias hides the actual DS role */
color: var(--foreground);
background: var(--background);
background: var(--card);
color: var(--muted-foreground);
border-color: var(--border);
background: var(--sidebar);
background: var(--accent);
background: var(--destructive);

/* ✅ GOOD — DS token is explicit */
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-neutral-primary);
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-quaternary);
border-color: var(--ds-border-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-neutral-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-brand-primary);
background: var(--ds-background-error-primary);
```

### Alias → DS token mapping (quick reference)

| Alias | DS Token |
|---|---|
| `--foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--background` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` |
| `--card` / `--card-foreground` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` / `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--popover` / `--popover-foreground` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` / `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--primary` | `--ds-background-brand-primary` |
| `--primary-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed` |
| `--secondary` | `--ds-background-neutral-secondary` |
| `--secondary-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |
| `--muted` | `--ds-background-neutral-quaternary` |
| `--muted-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-quaternary` |
| `--accent` | `--ds-background-brand-primary` |
| `--accent-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed` |
| `--destructive` | `--ds-background-error-primary` |
| `--destructive-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed` |
| `--border` | `--ds-border-neutral-primary` |
| `--input` / `--input-background` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` |
| `--ring` | `--ds-border-focused-primary` |
| `--sidebar` | `--ds-background-neutral-primary` |
| `--sidebar-foreground` | `--ds-text-neutral-primary` |

### Selected vs brand

| Role | Tokens |
|---|---|
| Actions / CTAs / header | `--ds-*-brand-*` (collapsed; purple under the hood) |
| Selected / active chrome | `--ds-*-selected-*` |
| Focus rings | `--ds-border-focused-*` via the `focus-ring` mixin (2px outline + 2px offset) |

## Color: no hardcoded hex values

Never write raw hex like `#fff`, `#292F36`, `#69788a`, etc. Pick the matching `--ds-*` token.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
color: #fff;
color: #292F36;

/* ✅ GOOD */
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-white-fixed);
color: var(--ds-text-neutral-black-fixed);
```

## Typography: use size tokens

Prefer the CADS ramp in `globals.css`:

| Token | Value |
|---|---|
| `--text-heading-xxl` / `--text-h1` | 48px |
| `--text-heading-xl` / `--text-h2` | 38px |
| `--text-heading-lg` / `--text-h3` | 28px |
| `--text-heading-md` / `--text-h4` | 24px |
| `--text-heading-sm` | 22px |
| `--text-heading-xs` / `--text-lg` | 20px |
| `--text-body-lg` / `--text-md` | 18px |
| `--text-body-md` / `--text-base` | 16px |
| `--text-body-sm` / `--text-sm` | 14px |
| `--text-body-xs` / `--text-label` | 12px |
| `--text-body-xxs` / `--text-xs` | 10px |

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
font-size: 12px;
font-size: 16px;
font-size: 24px;

/* ✅ GOOD */
font-size: var(--text-label);
font-size: var(--text-base);
font-size: var(--text-h4);
```

If a design truly requires a size not in this table, add a new token to `globals.css` rather than hard-coding the value.

## Typography: use weight and family tokens

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
font-weight: 600;
font-family: 'Figtree', sans-serif;

/* ✅ GOOD */
font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
font-family: var(--font-body);
```

Available weight tokens: `--font-weight-bold` (700), `--font-weight-semibold` (600), `--font-weight-medium` (500), `--font-weight-normal` (400).
Available family tokens: `--font-heading` (Space Grotesk), `--font-body` (Geist), `--font-mono` (Google Sans Code).

## Shape, spacing, shadows

- Radii: `--radius-sm` (6), `--radius-md` (8), `--radius-lg` (10), `--radius-round` (999)
- Spacing (forward-use): `--space-xxs` … `--space-xxxl`
- Shadows: `--shadow-sm` / `--shadow-md` / `--shadow-lg`

## SCSS files

When writing new SCSS, prefer `var(--ds-*)` over the SCSS `$color-*` variables in `_tokens.scss`.

## When to use mapped aliases

The **only** place mapped aliases belong is in `globals.css` itself (where they are defined) and in Tailwind utility classes (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`) which rely on the `@theme` block. In hand-written CSS/SCSS, always use the `--ds-*` form.


## Components

Always use shared and reusable components where available. Most importantly, always use the AppButton unless directed otherwise.

Always use the new FAIcon component and do not import icons needed for a view individually at the top of the file.
